# dvtm for tmux junkies

# basic

```sh
dvtm -m '^[' [FLAG]... [COMMAND]...
```

run each command in a separate window

## bindings

the default prefix for dvtm is `ctrl+g`. to set it to `escape` we invoke dvtm as
`dvtm -m '^['` or change its source

|  key   | action                                      |
| :----: | ------------------------------------------- |
|   c    | new pane                                    |
|   j    | move to pane below                          |
|   k    | move to pane above                          |
| enter  | toggle pane zoom (move to/from master area) |
| space  | cycle through tiling layouts                |
|   f    | change to vertical stack layout             |
|   g    | change to grid layout                       |
|   m    | maximize current pane                       |
| ctrl+x | close pane                                  |
|   d    | detach window                               |

## flags

| flag | use                                                                            |
| :--: | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
|  -v  | version info                                                                   |
|  -M  | toggle default mouse grabbing                                                  |
|  -m  | set prefix                                                                     |
|  -d  | time (in secs) before ncurses decides a char is not part of an escape sequence |
|  -h  | scrollback buffer size (lines)                                                 |
|  -t  | set immutable title                                                            |
|  -s  | listen to named pipe and display in status bar                                 |
|  -c  | listen to named pipe and execute incident commands                             |
